[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4964909973","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121343#issuecomment-4964909973","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121343","id":4964909973,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ-6DlQ","user":{"login":"almoandrioli-ai","id":260156588,"node_id":"U_kgDOD4GsrA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260156588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/almoandrioli-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-14T02:46:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-14T02:47:05Z","body":"I believe the issue may be related to HeightmapShape3D scaling. When I create a terrain at 1:1 (resolution 1024, size 1024) the heightmap scale is 1.0 and collisions are perfectly stable — no sinking or phantom bumps on my tests (but need more tests to confirm). However, when I create a larger terrain (for example resolution 1024, size 8192) the HeightmapShape3D uses a uniform scale of 8.0. In this case, vehicles start to experience collision artifacts such as false bumps and sinking. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4964909973/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4996715354","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121343#issuecomment-4996715354","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121343","id":4996715354,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKdPTWg","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-16T21:22:40Z","updated_at":"2026-07-16T21:22:40Z","body":"At first glance, you may be running into floating point precision errors. The terrain triangles are absolutely huge compared to the wheels of the vehicle:\n\n<img width=\"1909\" height=\"1077\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8a51367c-436c-4b8e-8315-2542fedcf736\" />\n\nAt this difference in scale it's hard to accurately detect the collision point. Especially at the speed at which the vehicle travels, a small error will result in a wheel popping through. If you up the scale of the terrain, you have to up the resolution of your height map as well:\n\n<img width=\"514\" height=\"593\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ae55b8d1-2cb2-4631-bde4-87fc58f3bbee\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4996715354/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5008845251","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121343#issuecomment-5008845251","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121343","id":5008845251,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKozpww","user":{"login":"almoandrioli-ai","id":260156588,"node_id":"U_kgDOD4GsrA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260156588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/almoandrioli-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/almoandrioli-ai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-18T00:36:37Z","updated_at":"2026-07-18T00:36:37Z","body":"Thanks for the detailed explanation, I really appreciate it. I understand, and I’m reducing the terrain scale so the triangles aren’t too large compared to the vehicle. However, I tested in the same scene using raycast-based wheels instead of RigidBody3D, and I didn’t encounter any collision detection issues. This makes me think the problem might be more specifically related to the interaction between RigidBody3D and HeightMapShape3D.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5008845251/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5011891841","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121343#issuecomment-5011891841","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121343","id":5011891841,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKrtmgQ","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-18T15:52:14Z","updated_at":"2026-07-18T15:52:14Z","body":"> However, I tested in the same scene using raycast-based wheels instead of RigidBody3D, and I didn’t encounter any collision detection issues.\n\nThe algorithm for colliding a ray with a triangle is much much simpler than the one for colliding a cylinder with a triangle. Therefore it is much less likely to fail due to floating point precision issues.\n\nIn the mean time I have confirmed that it is indeed a precision issue. I've managed to reproduce the issue in the Jolt framework. That shows in the frame prior to the bad frame that it has valid contact normals (red arrows):\n\n<img width=\"1924\" height=\"1134\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b9b2bd0b-9ebc-4e11-8e7a-451e0f2fa04c\" />\n\nThen the next frame shows that one of the wheels has detected a flipped contact normal (in wireframe more or else it is hidden in the wheel):\n\n<img width=\"1924\" height=\"1134\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6f4bc7b0-44f2-4e63-8ad6-f2656d9aaf50\" />\n\nThis causes it to get pushed through the floor the next frame and breaks the vehicle:\n\n<img width=\"1924\" height=\"1134\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/89be3fa5-cc0a-400b-a350-9f05f508c606\" />\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5011891841/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]